    "type": "code",
    "file": "main.go",
    "lines": [
     "var ErrNotFound = errors.New(\"not found\")",
     "",
     "type AgeError struct{ Age int }",
     "",
     "func (e AgeError) Error() string {",
     "  return fmt.Sprintf(\"bad age: %d\", e.Age)",
     "}"
    ],
    "highlight": [
     4
    ],
    "output": [
     "bad age: -3"
    ]
   },
   "face": "happy",
   "palette": "blue",
   "say": "First, a sentinel error, ErrNotFound, made with errors dot New. Second, any struct with an Error method is an error too. So AgeError prints bad age minus three."
  },
  {
   "title": [
    {
     "text": "Wrap it",
     "box": "yellow"
    },
    {
     "text": "with %w"
    }
   ],
   "image": {
    "type": "code",
    "file": "main.go",
    "lines": [
     "func find(id int) error {",
     "  if id != 1 {",
     "    return fmt.Errorf(",
     "      \"user %d: %w\", id, ErrNotFound)",
     "  }",
     "  return nil",
     "}",
     "",
     "err := find(7)",
     "fmt.Println(err)"
    ],
    "highlight": [
     2,
     3
    ],
    "output": [
     "user 7: not found"
    ]
   },
   "face": "thinking",
   "palette": "orange",
   "say": "Now find wraps ErrNotFound with fmt dot Errorf and percent w. It adds context, user seven, but keeps the original error inside."
  },
  {
   "title": [
    {
     "text": "errors.Is",
     "box": "yellow"
    },
    {
     "text": "vs =="
    }
   ],
   "image": {
    "type": "code",
    "file": "main.go",
    "lines": [
     "fmt.Println(errors.Is(err, ErrNotFound))",
     "fmt.Println(err == ErrNotFound)"
    ],
    "highlight": [
     0
    ],
    "output": [
     "true",
     "false"
    ]
   },
   "face": "happy",
   "palette": "purple",
   "say": "errors dot Is looks inside the wrap, so it says true. Double equals only compares the outside, so it says false. Use errors dot Is."
  },
